 ## Unreleased
 
+- Flash Next on CUDA: opt-in `TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_OVERLAP` runs a `--tp 2` prompt chunk of at least 2,048 rows as two halves whose expert exchanges run on a side stream and NCCL communicator under the other half's layer, `TF_FLASHNEXT_OWNER_NOCLEAR` skips the owner-slot pass's zero fill of y, and `TF_FLASHNEXT_OVERLAP_OUTPROJ` moves the out projection's gathers to the side stream too; with all three, cold prefill is 42 to 45% faster at 8K, 32K and 128K on 2x RTX PRO 6000 with every token unchanged, at about 2.15 GiB more a rank (`--parallel 14` at a 49152-token window); default serving is unchanged (#1).
+
 - Server: `/v1/metrics` reports a `tensorfold:open_connections` gauge, the client connections admitted over TCP or the Unix socket and not yet closed, including idle keep-alive ones (#3925). Thanks to @plotarmordev.
 
 - Tools: served checks reject unexercised draft, seed, cache, cancellation and logit comparisons, covered by 11 served and constraint regression tests, and benchmark receipts name vacuous comparisons (#3772, refs #2460). Thanks to @jschmied.
